WEBVTT

00:08.800 --> 01:05.760
Black Cat presents Peter Pan, by James Matthew Barry, adapted by Gina D. B. Clemon, copyright right, Black Cat Publishing. Chapter 1. The Darling Family. Wendy, John, and Michael with a lot of rooms and a garden outside. They live with their parents, Mr. and Mrs. Darling. The darlings are a happy family. Mr. and Mrs. Darling love their children very much.

01:08.180 --> 01:16.700
Wendy is the first child, and she is pretty. She has got long, blonde hair and blue eyes.

01:17.760 --> 01:35.680
John is the second child, and he is tall and thin. He has got brown hair and brown eyes, and he wears glasses. Michael is the third child, and he has got brown hair and blue eyes.

01:36.820 --> 01:45.170
The three children are very friendly. Wendy, John, and Michael like playing in the nursery.

01:45.220 --> 01:53.900
It is a big, sunny nursery, and there are pictures on the walls. There are a lot of toys in the nursery.

01:56.080 --> 02:15.140
The children have a nanny called Nana. She is a big Newfoundland dog. She is a wonderful nanny, and looks after the children. She loves them, and they love her. Her kennel is in the nursery.

02:16.980 --> 02:33.820
One evening, Mr. and Mrs. Darling put on some very nice clothes. They are going to a dinner party with their friends. Mrs. Darling goes to the nursery. The children are playing happily.

02:35.400 --> 02:43.820
Wendy sees her mother and says, What a lovely dress. Yes. Says John.

02:44.500 --> 02:51.450
You are wearing a beautiful dress. Thank you. Says Mrs. Darling.

02:51.500 --> 03:05.680
Your father and I are going to a dinner party this evening. Then she looks at Nana and says, Nana, it is almost half past eight. It is time to put the children to bed.

03:07.260 --> 03:13.450
Nana looks at Mrs. Darling with her big brown eyes and barks.

03:13.500 --> 03:20.440
Roof. Roof. She goes to the bathroom and turns on the hot water for Michael's bath.

03:21.960 --> 03:28.080
But Michael does not like having baths. No. Says little Michael.

03:29.040 --> 03:39.460
I don't want to have a bath, and I don't want to go to bed. Nana is a good nanny, and the children must listen to her.

03:40.500 --> 03:47.540
Michael has his bath. Then she gives the children their pajamas, and they are ready for bed now.

03:49.100 --> 03:52.560
Mrs. Darling comes to the nursery again and smiles.

03:53.460 --> 04:02.460
Good work, Nana. The children are ready for bed. Nana looks at Mrs. Darling and barks.

04:03.460 --> 04:06.360
Then she goes and sits near her cannel.

04:07.420 --> 04:11.640
I can hear a noise outside the window. Says Wendy.

04:12.380 --> 04:16.460
Yes. Says John. I can hear it too.

04:17.700 --> 04:22.460
Mrs. Darling goes to the nursery window and is very surprised.

04:23.460 --> 04:27.940
She sees a young boy outside the nursery window.

04:29.160 --> 04:33.080
Nana barks loudly and shuts the window quickly.

04:34.160 --> 04:39.200
The boy's shadow falls on the floor, and the young boy flies away.

04:41.320 --> 04:44.280
Who's there? asks Mrs. Darling.

04:45.640 --> 04:50.940
She opens the window and looks outside, but she can't see anything.

04:51.700 --> 04:55.480
How strange. There's no one here.

04:56.260 --> 05:01.240
She turns around and sees the boy's shadow on the floor.

05:02.120 --> 05:05.040
Wendy, John and Michael see it too.

05:06.800 --> 05:07.920
What's that?

05:09.000 --> 05:12.340
They ask, looking at the shadow on the floor.

05:13.180 --> 05:16.980
It's the poor boy's shadow. Says Mrs. Darling.

05:17.900 --> 05:20.800
What can we do with it? asks Wendy.

05:22.060 --> 05:25.320
Let's put it in the drawer. Says Mrs. Darling.

05:26.540 --> 05:28.040
The children get into bed.

05:29.000 --> 05:31.140
Mr. Darling takes Nana to the garden.

05:32.160 --> 05:35.600
Then he goes to the sitting room and waits for Mrs. Darling.

05:36.860 --> 05:42.220
Mrs. Darling sings to Wendy, John and Michael and kisses them.

05:43.340 --> 05:45.760
She is a wonderful mother.

05:47.160 --> 05:49.720
Soon the three children are sleeping.

05:51.580 --> 05:53.980
Mr. and Mrs. Darling go to their bedroom.

05:55.260 --> 05:58.500
They put on their coats and go to the dinner party.

06:01.780 --> 06:02.380
London.

06:04.020 --> 06:09.480
The story you are reading starts in London in the early 1900s.

06:10.440 --> 06:15.100
London is a wonderful city and it is the capital of the United Kingdom.

06:16.320 --> 06:20.300
Today almost eight million people live there.

06:22.160 --> 06:24.580
London is a very green city.

06:25.680 --> 06:27.620
There are more than three hundred parks.

06:28.640 --> 06:34.420
Hyde Park is a very big park with more than four thousand trees.

06:35.600 --> 06:40.980
You can go biking in the park or you can ride a boat on the Serpentine lake.

06:41.780 --> 06:45.320
In the summer there are music concerts in the park.

06:46.840 --> 06:53.580
In Kensington Gardens there is a statue of Peter Pan and a lot of visitors go and see it.

06:54.820 --> 06:59.320
The River Thames runs through the city and a lot of bridges cross it.

07:00.320 --> 07:05.040
You can take a lovely boat ride on the River Thames and ride under Tower Bridge.

07:06.120 --> 07:11.700
Big Ben is the name of an enormous clock on top of a tall tower.

07:12.680 --> 07:18.520
You can see the tower and the clock next to the houses of Parliament on the River Thames.

07:20.100 --> 07:23.020
The Tower of London is a very old tower.

07:23.900 --> 07:27.780
It was built between ten seventy and eleven hundred.

07:28.620 --> 07:32.420
You can visit the tower and see the Queen's crown jewels.

07:34.140 --> 07:38.860
There are always a lot of interesting things to do and see in London.

07:40.000 --> 07:45.020
There are more than two hundred and forty important museums and many of them are free.

07:46.020 --> 07:49.100
There are also a lot of important theatres.

07:52.260 --> 08:00.000
Chapter Two Peter's Shadow Everything is dark and silent in the nursery.

08:01.020 --> 08:05.300
Wendy John and Michael are sleeping and dreaming.

08:06.720 --> 08:10.980
Outside the nursery window there is a small ball of light.

08:12.400 --> 08:13.960
The nursery window is open.

08:15.060 --> 08:22.570
Suddenly the small ball of light comes into the nursery through the window and flies around.

08:22.620 --> 08:27.540
It is a fairy called Tinkerbell.

08:28.420 --> 08:31.640
She is very small and lovely.

08:34.540 --> 08:38.800
She is looking for something inside the nursery.

08:40.380 --> 08:47.360
After a moment a young boy comes into the nursery through the open window and looks around.

08:48.700 --> 08:52.180
Tink, he says, where are you?

08:53.100 --> 08:56.660
Where is my shadow? Please find it.

08:57.800 --> 09:02.460
Tinkerbell flies around the nursery and stops near a drawer.

09:03.660 --> 09:07.460
She opens it carefully and finds his shadow.

09:08.280 --> 09:09.600
Then she gives it to him.

09:11.100 --> 09:14.690
Thank you Tink, says the boy happily.

09:14.740 --> 09:18.420
He goes to the bathroom and gets some soap.

09:19.120 --> 09:23.540
Now I can put the shadow on my feet with some soap.

09:24.480 --> 09:28.320
He tries to stick it on his feet, but he can't.

09:29.080 --> 09:32.600
Why can't I put my shadow on my feet?

09:33.340 --> 09:33.780
He thinks.

09:35.100 --> 09:37.560
Now I haven't got a shadow.

09:38.740 --> 09:42.030
He is very sad and starts to cry.

09:42.080 --> 09:47.520
Wendy hears the boy crying and she wakes up.

09:48.640 --> 09:52.000
She sees a young boy, but she is not afraid.

09:53.180 --> 09:56.400
He has got red hair and a friendly face.

09:57.420 --> 10:01.400
His clothes are made of green leaves. She thinks.

10:02.320 --> 10:05.320
What's this boy doing in the nursery?

10:06.700 --> 10:09.650
Little boy, why are you crying?

10:09.700 --> 10:16.280
Wendy asks. The boy smiles and asks, What's your name?

10:17.260 --> 10:21.680
My name's Wendy Moira Angela Darling.

10:22.480 --> 10:23.520
And what's yours?

10:24.500 --> 10:25.240
Peter Pan.

10:25.880 --> 10:29.280
Is that all? Asks Wendy looking at him.

10:29.900 --> 10:32.700
Yes, that's all. Says Peter.

10:33.780 --> 10:37.860
Then he thinks, my name is very short.

10:38.860 --> 10:44.680
Wendy looks at his shadow on the floor and says, Is this your shadow?

10:45.320 --> 10:47.100
Yes. Says Peter.

10:47.880 --> 10:49.460
But I can't put it on.

10:50.060 --> 10:53.960
Wendy smiles and says, I can sew it on.

10:54.820 --> 10:56.120
Can you?

10:56.900 --> 11:00.280
Oh please do it. Says Peter happily.

11:01.460 --> 11:07.010
Wendy gets her big sewing basket and so's on Peter's shadow carefully.

11:07.060 --> 11:10.660
Peter looks at her and is very glad.

11:11.640 --> 11:15.500
After a few minutes Wendy says, I finished.

11:16.660 --> 11:19.160
Now you've got your shadow again.

11:20.140 --> 11:23.720
Peter looks at the floor and he can see his shadow.

11:24.600 --> 11:27.820
He is happy and he dances around the nursery.

11:30.020 --> 11:31.500
Thank you Wendy.

11:32.200 --> 11:35.030
He says, You're a wonderful girl.

11:35.080 --> 11:39.000
Do you really think so? Asks Wendy.

11:39.640 --> 11:43.040
Yes, I do. Says Peter, looking at Wendy.

11:44.320 --> 11:47.860
Wendy smiles and gives Peter a kiss on the cheek.

11:48.740 --> 11:50.580
Oh. Says Peter.

11:51.420 --> 11:52.240
That's nice.

11:53.300 --> 11:56.880
How old are you Peter? Asks Wendy.

11:58.040 --> 12:01.430
Peter thinks for a moment and says, I don't know.

12:01.480 --> 12:05.240
But I'm young and I don't want to grow up.

12:05.820 --> 12:08.240
I don't want to become an adult.

12:09.080 --> 12:13.800
I want to be a boy forever and have lots of fun.

12:15.120 --> 12:18.320
Wendy listens to Peter and is surprised.

12:19.240 --> 12:21.520
Then Peter looks for his fairy.

12:22.720 --> 12:26.200
Suddenly he hears a noise and looks in a drawer.

12:27.320 --> 12:29.050
Little Tinkerbell flies out.

12:29.100 --> 12:31.660
Wendy is happy to see a fairy.

12:32.880 --> 12:33.980
But Tinkerbell is afraid.

12:34.880 --> 12:36.820
She hides behind the big clock.

12:37.780 --> 12:40.800
Where do you live Peter? Asks Wendy.

12:41.640 --> 12:46.280
I sometimes live in Kensington Gardens. Says Peter.

12:47.300 --> 12:51.460
But most of the time I live in Neverland with the Lost Boys.

12:52.520 --> 12:54.640
Wendy does not understand.

12:56.180 --> 12:56.940
Neverland?

12:57.800 --> 12:59.560
The Lost Boys?

13:00.480 --> 13:01.580
Who are they?

13:02.240 --> 13:07.480
The Lost Boys haven't got a mother or father. Says Peter.

13:08.260 --> 13:11.920
They're alone in the world and they live in Neverland.

13:12.580 --> 13:13.900
I'm their captain.

13:14.680 --> 13:15.200
Oh.

13:15.780 --> 13:20.020
Neverland sounds like a wonderful place. Says Wendy.

13:20.960 --> 13:22.680
It is. Says Peter.

13:23.320 --> 13:25.330
And we have lots of fun there.

13:25.380 --> 13:28.860
In Neverland, we fight the pirates.

13:29.740 --> 13:33.920
We swim in the lagoon with beautiful mermaids.

13:34.480 --> 13:38.400
A lot of lovely fairies live in the trees in the forest.

13:39.140 --> 13:40.000
They're my friends.

13:40.640 --> 13:42.720
What fun? Says Wendy.

13:43.520 --> 13:47.760
Well, I must go back to Neverland now. Says Peter.

13:48.320 --> 13:50.720
I must tell the Lost Boys a story.

13:51.420 --> 13:53.380
You know, they love stories.

13:54.220 --> 13:58.000
I know a lot of stories. Says Wendy.

13:59.020 --> 14:02.040
Then come with me to Neverland. Says Peter.

14:02.840 --> 14:04.860
You can tell us lots of stories.

14:05.680 --> 14:09.200
And you can see the beautiful mermaids in the lagoon.

14:09.800 --> 14:11.280
Come with me.

14:11.720 --> 14:13.260
We all want a mother.

14:13.920 --> 14:14.280
Oh.

14:14.800 --> 14:17.160
I can't come with you. Says Wendy.

14:17.740 --> 14:18.640
I can't fly.

14:19.380 --> 14:22.720
I can teach you to fly. Says Peter.

14:23.240 --> 14:24.520
It's very easy.

14:25.180 --> 14:30.400
Can you teach John and Michael to fly too? asks Wendy.

14:31.080 --> 14:32.820
Of course. Says Peter.

14:33.920 --> 14:37.450
Wendy goes to John and Michael and says...

14:37.500 --> 14:38.020
Wake up.

14:38.680 --> 14:39.240
Quickly.

14:40.580 --> 14:41.500
Peter Pan is here.

14:42.240 --> 14:43.760
He's from Neverland.

14:44.640 --> 14:45.780
It's a fun place.

14:46.560 --> 14:48.570
John and Michael wake up.

14:48.620 --> 14:50.880
And they are very surprised.

14:51.640 --> 14:55.700
We can go to Neverland with him. Says Wendy.

14:56.400 --> 14:58.280
But we must learn to fly.

14:59.080 --> 15:01.740
That's difficult. Says John.

15:02.420 --> 15:04.580
No, it's not. Says Peter.

15:05.520 --> 15:06.060
Look at me.

15:07.040 --> 15:09.380
Peter flies around the nursery.

15:10.260 --> 15:11.460
And the children look at him.

15:12.220 --> 15:14.530
They are excited and try to fly.

15:14.580 --> 15:18.460
But they fall on the beds and on the floor.

15:19.460 --> 15:20.620
It's impossible.

15:22.320 --> 15:23.710
They say...

15:23.760 --> 15:28.620
You need some fairy dust. Says Peter laughing.

15:29.700 --> 15:31.960
He puts some fairy dust on their heads.

15:32.940 --> 15:34.220
Now try again.

15:35.620 --> 15:38.100
Wendy, John and Michael can fly now.

15:39.080 --> 15:40.960
And they are very happy.

15:42.860 --> 15:47.140
Look, I can fly. Says Wendy.

15:47.700 --> 15:52.100
We can too. Say John and Michael.

15:52.660 --> 15:57.540
Now we can go to Neverland with Peter. Says Wendy happily.

15:58.780 --> 16:00.980
Tink. Says Peter.

16:01.960 --> 16:04.020
Show us the way to Neverland.

16:05.400 --> 16:09.640
They follow Tinkerbell and fly out of the nursery window.

16:10.700 --> 16:13.240
There are a lot of stars in the night sky.

16:14.640 --> 16:18.460
In the garden, Nana looks at the sky and barks loudly.

16:20.060 --> 16:20.360
Wooo!

16:22.440 --> 16:27.000
Mr. and Mrs. Darling return from the dinner party at 11 o'clock.

16:28.160 --> 16:29.080
They go to the nursery.

16:30.580 --> 16:31.380
But it is empty.

16:32.900 --> 16:34.220
Where are the children?

16:37.100 --> 16:38.680
Chapter 3.

16:39.560 --> 16:40.480
Neverland.

16:41.760 --> 16:45.560
Wendy, John and Michael fly over London.

16:46.560 --> 16:49.600
They see the river Thames and Tower Bridge.

16:50.660 --> 16:52.940
There are hundreds of lights in the city.

16:53.980 --> 17:03.680
Then they fly over big cities, small towns, tall mountains, green forests, and blue seas.

17:04.660 --> 17:08.680
At last, they see an island in the sea below them.

17:09.540 --> 17:12.320
It is a beautiful island.

17:13.680 --> 17:17.980
That's Neverland. Says Peter looking down at the island.

17:18.960 --> 17:20.380
It is a sunny day now.

17:21.160 --> 17:21.700
But it's Wendy.

17:23.340 --> 17:27.400
Neverland. Say the children happily.

17:28.260 --> 17:30.180
Look, John. Says Wendy.

17:30.760 --> 17:32.020
There's the lagoon.

17:32.600 --> 17:35.960
And there's the big forest. Says Michael.

17:37.460 --> 17:39.520
The three children are excited.

17:41.000 --> 17:45.760
The lost boys live in the green forest in a secret underground home.

17:46.740 --> 17:48.480
There are six lost boys.

17:49.280 --> 17:56.460
And their names are Curly, Nibs, Tootles, Slightly Soiled and the Twins.

17:57.460 --> 18:00.520
They are waiting for Peter in the underground home.

18:02.060 --> 18:05.040
Suddenly they hear the voices of the pirates.

18:06.180 --> 18:08.660
I thought I'm certain there were five of them.

18:08.960 --> 18:10.620
You want your eyes examined in boy?

18:10.900 --> 18:11.480
Pass me that rope.

18:12.120 --> 18:16.440
I can hear the pirates. Says Tootles.

18:16.940 --> 18:18.260
They're in the forest.

18:19.360 --> 18:23.880
I'm afraid of them. Says Slightly Soiled.

18:24.660 --> 18:27.600
What can we do? Asks Curly.

18:28.280 --> 18:31.700
I'm not afraid of the pirates. Says Nibs.

18:32.600 --> 18:34.700
He goes out of the underground home.

18:35.620 --> 18:38.900
He hides behind a big tree and looks around.

18:40.020 --> 18:41.820
He sees the terrible pirates.

18:42.800 --> 18:47.560
They are walking in the forest and they are big and strong.

18:48.440 --> 18:52.480
They live on a pirate ship called the Jolly Roger.

18:53.720 --> 18:56.640
The pirates captain is James Hook.

18:57.680 --> 19:01.540
He is a very bad pirate.

19:02.680 --> 19:08.840
He has got black eyes, black hair and a big black beard.

19:10.080 --> 19:11.840
He hates Peter Pan.

19:12.600 --> 19:14.340
He has got only one hand.

19:15.300 --> 19:17.640
The other hand is a hook.

19:18.620 --> 19:23.560
In the past Peter cut off Captain Hook's right arm during a fight.

19:24.940 --> 19:28.920
A crocodile ate the arm because crocodiles are always hungry.

19:30.340 --> 19:35.620
Now the crocodile follows Captain Hook everywhere because he wants to eat him.

19:36.760 --> 19:40.480
The crocodile has an alarm clock in its stomach.

19:41.480 --> 19:44.680
Captain Hook can always hear it.

19:46.400 --> 19:53.340
We must find Peter Pan and the lost boys. Says Captain Hook angrily.

19:54.260 --> 19:58.520
I know they live in this forest, but where?

20:00.320 --> 20:05.840
The pirates look everywhere, but they cannot find the secret underground home.

20:06.840 --> 20:13.960
Suddenly Captain Hook hears the alarm clock tick tock tick tock.

20:15.840 --> 20:19.940
The crocodile is near Christ Captain Hook.

20:20.680 --> 20:21.800
He wants to eat me.

20:22.380 --> 20:24.380
We must leave the forest quickly.

20:26.020 --> 20:29.260
He runs away and the pirates follow him.

20:30.000 --> 20:33.840
Soon some American Indians come to the forest.

20:34.500 --> 20:38.640
They walk silently and carry bows and arrows.

20:39.760 --> 20:41.160
They are looking for the pirates.

20:42.300 --> 20:43.780
The pirates are their enemies.

20:45.100 --> 20:47.240
Their leader is Tiger Lily.

20:48.320 --> 20:52.100
She is the lovely daughter of the American Indian chief.

20:53.040 --> 20:54.780
She likes Peter Pan a lot.

20:55.800 --> 20:59.680
The Indians cannot find the pirates and they soon go away.

21:00.540 --> 21:05.520
Now the lost boys can leave the underground home and play in the forest.

21:06.760 --> 21:12.420
Nibs looks at the sky and says, Look, there's a white bird in the sky.

21:13.160 --> 21:18.660
The lost boys look at the sky and Curly asks, Is it really a bird?

21:19.720 --> 21:23.200
Of course it's a bird. Says Tinkerbell.

21:23.880 --> 21:27.760
It's a windy bird. You must shoot it.

21:29.380 --> 21:32.260
Sometimes Tinkerbell is a bad fairy.

21:33.360 --> 21:36.940
She knows that it is windy, but she doesn't like her.

21:37.920 --> 21:40.840
Nibs takes his bow and arrow and looks at the sky.

21:41.600 --> 21:44.640
He shoots windy and she falls to the ground.

21:45.840 --> 21:47.980
Then the lost boys go and see windy.

21:49.500 --> 21:51.100
She's not a bird.

21:52.600 --> 21:56.480
They say, She's a lovely girl.

21:58.260 --> 22:04.300
Peter flies down with John and Michael and asks, Where's windy?

22:05.120 --> 22:08.320
Tutels says, Here she is.

22:08.740 --> 22:13.720
Peter goes to her and asks, Wendy, are you all right?

22:14.460 --> 22:18.180
Wendy slowly opens her eyes and smiles at Peter.

22:18.900 --> 22:21.110
Yes, I'm all right.

22:21.160 --> 22:27.020
She says, I'm lucky because the arrow hit the button of my night dress.

22:27.940 --> 22:30.600
The lost boys are very sorry.

22:31.300 --> 22:34.340
Poor Wendy. Says Curly.

22:34.960 --> 22:36.240
What can we do?

22:37.460 --> 22:41.480
I've got a good idea. Says slightly soiled.

22:42.460 --> 22:45.180
We can build her a little house.

22:46.020 --> 22:50.360
When the little house is ready, the lost boys go and tell Wendy.

22:51.040 --> 22:55.820
Come and see the little house, Wendy. Says Tutels.

22:56.920 --> 23:00.980
Do you like it? Ask the lost boys.

23:01.660 --> 23:05.480
Yes, I do. Says Wendy happily.

23:06.180 --> 23:07.800
It's a nice little house.

23:08.640 --> 23:09.360
Thank you.

23:10.100 --> 23:14.860
Wendy, Can you be our mother now? asks nibs.

23:15.520 --> 23:19.960
Can you tell us bedtime stories before we go to bed?

23:20.840 --> 23:24.040
Yes, please. Says Tutels.

23:24.600 --> 23:26.800
Come and be our mother.

23:27.820 --> 23:30.080
Of course. Says Wendy.

23:31.060 --> 23:34.780
Come in and I can tell you the story of Cinderella.

23:36.220 --> 23:41.340
They listen to Wendy's story and like it a lot.

23:45.160 --> 23:47.000
Fairies and their magic.

23:48.120 --> 23:53.480
People all over the world have stories about fairies and their magic.

23:54.440 --> 23:59.260
Some of these stories are very old and some of them are called fairy tales.

24:00.380 --> 24:06.460
Fairies are part of the British, Irish, Northern European and old cultures.

24:07.680 --> 24:11.680
In Peter Pan, Tinkerbell is Peter's fairy.

24:13.100 --> 24:16.600
Peter says that the fairies in Neverland are his good friends.

24:17.980 --> 24:22.380
In Pinocchio, there is a kind fairy called the Blue Fairy.

24:23.360 --> 24:24.960
She always helps Pinocchio.

24:26.200 --> 24:30.640
In Cinderella, a fairy godmother is Cinderella's good friend.

24:31.640 --> 24:35.520
There are fairies in one of William Shakespeare's plays too.

24:36.440 --> 24:43.320
In A Midsummer Night's Dream, Oberon and Titania are the king and queen of the fairies.

24:43.820 --> 24:47.940
They live in the forest and are important characters in the play.

24:49.520 --> 24:52.320
What some people say about fairies.

24:53.040 --> 24:55.230
They are small and have wings.

24:55.280 --> 25:00.900
They live in the forest, in trees, in flowers and in gardens.

25:02.000 --> 25:05.600
They are sometimes good and sometimes bad.

25:06.520 --> 25:07.220
They are magic.

25:08.120 --> 25:10.860
They can do good things and bad things.

25:14.200 --> 25:25.440
Chapter 4 Danger in the Lagoon Peter, Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys often go to the Mermaid's Lagoon.

25:26.420 --> 25:28.460
The water is blue and beautiful.

25:29.520 --> 25:32.520
They like swimming and playing in the Blue Lagoon.

25:33.740 --> 25:38.140
Beautiful mermaids live here and they are Peter's friends.

25:38.960 --> 25:42.400
They have got long hair and are very pretty.

25:43.340 --> 25:50.640
They play mermaid games and then sit on marooners' rock and comb their long hair.

25:51.580 --> 25:54.880
They sit in the sun and talk and laugh.

25:55.800 --> 26:02.120
The children like the mermaids and John says, I want to catch a mermaid.

26:02.620 --> 26:07.540
He tries, but the mermaid jumps into the water and swims away.

26:08.260 --> 26:09.320
Everyone laughs.

26:14.740 --> 26:19.420
It's very difficult to catch a mermaid. Says Peter.

26:20.200 --> 26:25.360
Suddenly Peter hears a noise and says, The pirates are coming.

26:26.040 --> 26:27.000
I can hear them.

26:27.700 --> 26:32.820
John, Michael and the Lost Boys jump into the water and swim away.

26:33.540 --> 26:35.160
They are afraid of the pirates.

26:36.180 --> 26:37.550
But Wendy stays with Peter.

26:37.600 --> 26:40.780
They hide behind marooners' rock.

26:42.140 --> 26:46.540
A small boat with two pirates is coming to the lagoon.

26:47.420 --> 26:49.360
One pirate is Smee.

26:49.820 --> 26:52.260
He is old and wears glasses.

26:53.740 --> 26:55.740
The other pirate is Starkey.

26:56.520 --> 26:59.080
He is young and has got a long nose.

27:00.300 --> 27:04.800
Tiger Lily is on the boat and she is a prisoner of the pirates.

27:06.260 --> 27:10.400
Let's leave her on this rock. Says Smee.

27:10.780 --> 27:14.520
When the sea rises, she's going to die.

27:16.120 --> 27:18.340
The two pirates laugh loudly.

27:19.400 --> 27:22.140
It is almost night and it is dark.

27:28.600 --> 27:29.990
Poor Tiger Lily.

27:30.040 --> 27:31.440
Thanks Peter.

27:31.960 --> 27:34.160
She is our good friend.

27:34.900 --> 27:36.340
I must save her.

27:37.040 --> 27:38.700
But what can I do?

27:39.640 --> 27:44.240
He thinks for a minute and then imitates Captain Hook's voice.

27:45.540 --> 27:49.420
Cut the ropes and let Tiger Lily go.

27:50.360 --> 27:52.120
Do as I say Smee.

27:53.000 --> 27:54.180
Let her go.

27:55.180 --> 28:00.380
The two pirates hear Captain Hook's voice and are very surprised.

28:01.620 --> 28:04.880
They look at each other and then they look around.

28:05.840 --> 28:08.520
Starkey says Smee.

28:08.740 --> 28:11.620
Can you hear Hook's voice?

28:12.400 --> 28:15.760
Yes. Says Starkey looking around.

28:16.440 --> 28:18.700
But I don't see Hook.

28:19.420 --> 28:23.090
We must listen to Hook and cut the ropes.

28:23.140 --> 28:25.080
Oops says Smee.

28:25.400 --> 28:28.640
Are you sure? Ask Starkey.

28:29.200 --> 28:32.660
Of course I'm sure. Says Smee.

28:33.320 --> 28:36.420
Starkey gets a knife and cuts the rope.

28:37.240 --> 28:38.520
Tiger Lily is free.

28:39.500 --> 28:42.200
She jumps into the water and swims away.

28:43.840 --> 28:50.260
Captain Hook is on his ship, the Jolly Roger, and he sees everything.

28:50.920 --> 28:55.060
He is very angry because Tiger Lily is free.

28:56.360 --> 29:02.020
Peter Pan is very clever. thinks Captain Hook.

29:03.180 --> 29:05.260
I must fight him.

29:06.520 --> 29:11.120
Captain Hook jumps into the water and swims to the rock.

29:12.100 --> 29:13.000
He fights with Peter.

29:14.160 --> 29:15.260
It is a long fight.

29:16.240 --> 29:19.190
Captain Hook hurts Peter with his big hook.

29:19.240 --> 29:22.200
But Peter does not stop fighting.

29:23.200 --> 29:23.800
He is brave.

29:25.120 --> 29:27.140
At last Peter wins the fight.

29:28.060 --> 29:32.100
Captain Hook is angry and swims back to the Jolly Roger.

29:33.180 --> 29:37.040
Peter and Wendy are now alone on the rock.

29:37.860 --> 29:43.240
What a terrible fight Peter. Says Wendy looking at Peter's hand.

29:43.900 --> 29:47.410
His hand is badly hurt after the fight with Captain Hook.

29:47.460 --> 29:49.860
Yes, says Peter.

29:50.540 --> 29:53.820
But I'm not afraid of Hook or the pirates.

29:54.880 --> 29:58.800
You're a very brave boy. Says Wendy, smiling.

29:59.560 --> 30:01.400
Look, says Peter.

30:01.960 --> 30:05.960
The sea is rising and we are in great danger here.

30:06.580 --> 30:09.400
What can we do? asks Wendy.

30:10.040 --> 30:15.610
We must leave this rock immediately. Says Peter, looking at the sea.

30:15.660 --> 30:18.540
Oh Peter. Says Wendy.

30:19.280 --> 30:23.620
I can't swim or fly because I'm very tired.

30:24.260 --> 30:25.680
Peter thinks for a moment.

30:26.280 --> 30:28.900
He sees a big kite with a long tail.

30:29.660 --> 30:32.280
It is flying slowly over the lagoon.

30:32.980 --> 30:41.640
He quickly takes the tail of the kite and says, Wendy, hold on to this tail and fly away with the kite.

30:42.640 --> 30:45.540
Wendy flies away with the kite.

30:46.480 --> 30:48.580
The sea is rising quickly.

30:49.260 --> 30:49.800
Peter thinks.

30:50.480 --> 30:52.000
I must fly away.

30:53.080 --> 30:57.680
When Peter gets home, everyone is happy to see him.

31:01.120 --> 31:03.780
Chapter 5. A Secret Place

31:05.800 --> 31:10.390
The underground home is a secret place in the big forest.

31:10.440 --> 31:15.560
It is a safe place because no one knows where it is.

31:16.540 --> 31:19.260
There is only one big room with a fireplace.

31:20.640 --> 31:23.180
It is a happy, warm home.

31:24.540 --> 31:27.120
Wendy, John and Michael are very happy there.

31:28.220 --> 31:30.260
Wendy is a wonderful mother.

31:31.240 --> 31:33.560
She cooks and so's for everyone.

31:34.680 --> 31:39.360
Every evening, after dinner, everyone sits in front of the fireplace.

31:40.040 --> 31:42.820
Wendy tells great bedtime stories.

31:44.200 --> 31:50.000
The lost boys love these stories and are happy because they finally have a mother.

31:51.360 --> 31:55.980
John and Michael are happy because there is an exciting adventure every day.

31:57.160 --> 31:58.280
They are never bored.

31:59.860 --> 32:01.680
Peter Pan is the perfect father.

32:02.580 --> 32:05.940
He brings home food and protects his family.

32:06.940 --> 32:10.900
He and Wendy play games with the children and laugh with them.

32:11.780 --> 32:14.540
Everyone is having a wonderful time.

32:16.040 --> 32:21.280
But in London, Mr. and Mrs. Darling are not happy.

32:22.140 --> 32:26.980
They are very sad because they can't find their three children.

32:28.300 --> 32:29.920
And Nana is sad too.

32:31.420 --> 32:33.920
Where are our three children?

32:34.800 --> 32:36.000
They think.

32:37.320 --> 32:40.260
Wendy sometimes thinks about her parents.

32:41.360 --> 32:44.310
One evening, she says...

32:44.360 --> 32:49.500
This evening, I'm going to tell you a new bedtime story.

32:50.360 --> 32:52.120
It takes place in England.

32:53.760 --> 32:58.420
Everyone sits down in front of the fireplace and listens to her.

32:59.420 --> 33:03.340
In the city of London, there are two parents.

33:04.340 --> 33:09.100
They're very sad because they can't find their three children.

33:09.960 --> 33:14.500
Every night, they leave the nursery window open.

33:15.460 --> 33:17.520
They want their children to return.

33:18.680 --> 33:23.840
They wait and wait, but their three children don't return.

33:24.840 --> 33:28.900
These poor parents are terribly sad.

33:29.960 --> 33:33.540
But Wendy... Say John and Michael.

33:34.160 --> 33:37.040
That's the story of our parents.

33:38.260 --> 33:42.130
Peter listens to the story and says...

33:42.180 --> 33:48.180
Sometimes parents forget their children and other children take their place.

33:49.300 --> 33:52.380
Wendy, John and Michael are surprised.

33:53.840 --> 33:54.580
They look at Peter.

33:55.520 --> 33:58.320
Are you sure, Peter? asks Wendy.

33:59.080 --> 34:01.720
Yes, I'm sure, says Peter.

34:02.440 --> 34:08.680
Perhaps there are other children in our nursery and in our beds. Says Wendy.

34:10.540 --> 34:14.500
John, Michael, we must go home immediately.

34:15.620 --> 34:19.650
John and Michael look at Wendy and say...

34:19.700 --> 34:21.710
Do we really have to go?

34:21.760 --> 34:25.960
Yes, we must go home. Says Wendy.

34:26.680 --> 34:29.540
Quickly, we haven't got much time.

34:30.280 --> 34:35.720
But we're happy here in Neverland with Peter and the Lost Boys. Says John.

34:36.380 --> 34:40.400
There's a new adventure every day. Says Michael.

34:40.960 --> 34:43.780
And we're never bored. Says John.

34:44.740 --> 34:46.840
Neverland is a wonderful place.

34:47.760 --> 34:51.640
Oh, Wendy. Say the Lost Boys.

34:53.140 --> 34:55.400
Please don't go away.

34:56.420 --> 34:57.900
Don't leave us.

34:58.860 --> 35:03.210
Wendy looks at the Lost Boys and says...

35:03.260 --> 35:04.640
Please don't be sad.

35:05.500 --> 35:08.120
You can come to London and live with us.

35:08.780 --> 35:11.400
You can be part of the Darling family.

35:12.660 --> 35:16.600
Oh, Wendy. Say the Lost Boys.

35:17.560 --> 35:18.820
Thank you.

35:19.540 --> 35:20.520
That's wonderful.

35:22.340 --> 35:26.620
We can have a real family in London.

35:29.220 --> 35:32.880
Nibs and tutels jump up and down and laugh.

35:34.080 --> 35:36.400
The other Lost Boys dance around the room.

35:37.400 --> 35:38.620
They are very happy.

35:39.660 --> 35:41.940
Peter is not happy.

35:42.680 --> 35:45.180
I'm not coming with you to London.

35:45.920 --> 35:48.980
Everyone is surprised and looks at him.

35:49.660 --> 35:51.800
Why? asks Wendy.

35:52.680 --> 35:56.060
I don't want to grow up. Says Peter.

35:56.980 --> 35:59.600
I don't want to become an adult.

36:00.740 --> 36:02.400
I want to be a boy forever.

36:03.440 --> 36:05.740
But Peter. Says Wendy.

36:06.700 --> 36:09.070
All boys and girls grow up.

36:09.120 --> 36:11.460
They become adults.

36:12.180 --> 36:15.120
No. Says Peter angrily.

36:15.980 --> 36:18.040
I don't want to grow up.

36:18.700 --> 36:21.480
You can go, but I'm not coming.

36:22.620 --> 36:25.300
He turns around and looks at the wall.

36:26.900 --> 36:34.820
Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys say goodbye to Peter and leave the underground home.

36:36.200 --> 36:38.820
They start to walk in the forest.

36:40.220 --> 36:43.920
But they don't know that the pirates are hiding behind the trees.

36:44.980 --> 36:46.360
They are waiting for them.

36:47.300 --> 36:50.060
Suddenly the pirates jump out of the forest.

36:51.180 --> 36:54.640
The children are very surprised and try to run away.

36:55.660 --> 36:57.520
But there are a lot of pirates.

36:58.840 --> 37:00.860
And they take the children to the Jolly Roger.

37:02.760 --> 37:07.580
Peter is inside the underground home and he does not hear anything.

37:08.960 --> 37:15.760
He sits in front of the fireplace and thinks about Wendy, John and Michael and the Lost Boys.

37:17.080 --> 37:18.600
He is sad without them.

37:20.020 --> 37:20.580
Tap.

37:21.280 --> 37:21.560
Tap.

37:21.840 --> 37:21.940
Tap.

37:23.220 --> 37:24.680
There is someone at the door.

37:25.820 --> 37:29.000
Peter goes to the door and asks, Who's there?

37:29.920 --> 37:31.480
He hears the sound of little bells.

37:33.820 --> 37:35.800
And opens the door.

37:36.760 --> 37:41.000
Tinkerbell flies in and says, The children are with the pirates.

37:42.280 --> 37:45.140
What do you mean, Tink? asks Peter.

37:46.120 --> 37:54.630
Wendy, John, Michael and the Lost Boys are on the Jolly Roger with Captain Hook. Says Tinkerbell.

37:54.680 --> 37:56.160
They're in danger.

37:57.020 --> 37:59.100
Oh no. Says Peter.

37:59.680 --> 38:01.260
We must save them.

38:01.820 --> 38:04.220
Let's go to the Jolly Roger quickly.

38:05.040 --> 38:07.140
I want to fight Hook.

38:08.180 --> 38:13.680
Peter and Tinkerbell leave the underground home and fly to the Jolly Roger.

38:16.340 --> 38:19.240
The Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children.

38:20.080 --> 38:26.160
In London, there is a hospital for sick children called the Great Ormond Street Hospital for Children.

38:27.260 --> 38:30.280
J.M. Barry likes children very much.

38:31.120 --> 38:33.260
He wants children to be well and happy.

38:34.160 --> 38:37.860
He often visits this hospital because he wants to help the children.

38:39.020 --> 38:40.530
Barry is a kind man.

38:40.580 --> 38:50.620
In 1929, he decides that all the money from book sales, films and theatre plays of Peter Pan goes to the hospital.

38:51.700 --> 38:52.940
And this continues today.

38:54.000 --> 38:58.940
This money helps the hospital, the children, the doctors and the nurses.

39:00.300 --> 39:04.580
The children at the hospital can watch the play Peter Pan once a year.

39:05.310 --> 39:08.680
This is a very happy moment for them.

39:11.240 --> 39:21.580
Chapter 6 The Pirate Ship The Jolly Roger is a big pirate ship in the bay near Kid's Creek.

39:22.380 --> 39:27.380
On the ship, there is a black flag with a white skull on it.

39:28.260 --> 39:29.860
It is the pirate's flag.

39:30.560 --> 39:32.500
It is night time.

39:33.480 --> 39:36.360
And there is a yellow moon in the dark sky.

39:38.160 --> 39:40.680
Peter sees the children on the pirate ship.

39:41.880 --> 39:43.520
They are prisoners of Captain Hook.

39:44.620 --> 39:45.840
And they are afraid of him.

39:47.080 --> 39:54.560
Captain Hook looks at the children and says, Peter Pan can't save you now.

39:55.680 --> 39:57.030
You're my prisoners.

39:57.080 --> 39:59.960
He starts to laugh.

40:00.920 --> 40:02.780
And the other pirates laugh too.

40:03.500 --> 40:04.140
Ha ha!

40:04.680 --> 40:08.720
Smee, come here. Says Captain Hook.

40:09.440 --> 40:12.460
Yes, sir. Says Smee.

40:13.020 --> 40:18.880
Get the plank ready for these children. Says Captain Hook.

40:19.620 --> 40:22.420
You're all right, sir. Says Smee.

40:22.840 --> 40:25.240
He goes to get the long plank.

40:26.240 --> 40:30.380
What's the plank? Asks John looking at Wendy.

40:31.760 --> 40:34.380
Ha ha! Laughs Captain Hook.

40:35.160 --> 40:38.460
You don't know what the plank is.

40:39.080 --> 40:43.260
You must all walk the plank tonight.

40:44.280 --> 40:48.020
I don't understand. Says John.

40:48.880 --> 40:50.800
First you walk the plank.

40:51.430 --> 40:57.000
And then you fall into the sea. Says Captain Hook.

40:57.620 --> 41:01.780
And in the sea there's a hungry crocodile.

41:02.360 --> 41:04.160
He wants to eat too.

41:04.880 --> 41:05.460
Ha ha!

41:07.040 --> 41:10.240
Oh no! Shout the children.

41:10.920 --> 41:12.180
They are afraid.

41:13.220 --> 41:19.640
But perhaps I can save two of you. Says Captain Hook.

41:20.100 --> 41:21.080
Looking at the children.

41:22.060 --> 41:24.360
I want two young pirates.

41:25.500 --> 41:27.740
Who wants to be a pirate?

41:29.280 --> 41:31.240
The lost boys look at John.

41:32.320 --> 41:35.350
And John looks at Michael and says...

41:35.400 --> 41:37.680
I don't want to walk the plank.

41:38.520 --> 41:42.000
I don't want to be food for that hungry crocodile.

41:42.740 --> 41:46.040
What do you mean, John? Asks Michael.

41:46.800 --> 41:48.520
Well. Says John.

41:49.240 --> 41:51.340
The life of a pirate is exciting.

41:52.420 --> 41:53.720
There are a lot of adventures.

41:54.540 --> 41:56.560
Let's be pirates, Michael.

41:57.220 --> 41:59.540
Michael does not know what to say.

42:00.400 --> 42:01.840
He and John look at Wendy.

42:02.880 --> 42:06.640
That's a terrible idea, John. Says Wendy.

42:07.420 --> 42:09.340
I'm surprised at you.

42:09.960 --> 42:15.460
Captain Hook moves his hook in front of their faces and laughs loudly.

42:16.480 --> 42:17.380
Ha ha!

42:17.820 --> 42:22.320
I want an answer from you. Says Captain Hook.

42:22.960 --> 42:25.320
Do you want to be pirates?

42:26.260 --> 42:28.420
Yes or no.

42:30.610 --> 42:34.740
John and Michael look at each other and then say...

42:35.400 --> 42:35.980
Never!

42:36.940 --> 42:40.680
What? Says Captain Hook angrily.

42:41.420 --> 42:45.900
Then you must walk the plank and die.

42:47.480 --> 42:48.860
Wendy is afraid.

42:49.780 --> 42:52.320
She loves her brothers and the lost boys.

42:53.340 --> 42:54.800
She has tears in her eyes.

42:55.880 --> 42:57.750
A pirate shouts...

42:57.800 --> 43:00.500
Who's the first to walk the plank?

43:01.540 --> 43:05.360
At that moment, everyone hears a loud noise.

43:06.280 --> 43:09.120
Tick, tock, tick, tock.

43:09.940 --> 43:10.580
Oh no.

43:11.760 --> 43:14.820
It's the crocodile. Says Captain Hook.

43:15.380 --> 43:17.540
He wants to eat me.

43:18.780 --> 43:24.580
His face is white and he runs to his cabin and hides there.

43:25.260 --> 43:30.780
The crocodile is hungry tonight. Says a pirate.

43:31.900 --> 43:34.580
Someone must walk the plank.

43:35.800 --> 43:42.160
Who's the first to walk the plank? asks me, looking at John and Michael.

43:43.060 --> 43:44.100
Let's go!

43:45.340 --> 43:50.420
Suddenly, Peter Pan arrives and Tinkerbell follows him.

43:51.380 --> 43:55.260
Wendy, John, Michael and the lost boys cheer happily.

43:56.260 --> 43:58.080
They are very happy to see him.

43:59.620 --> 44:00.660
Peter's here!

44:01.660 --> 44:02.620
They say.

44:03.320 --> 44:05.500
He's going to save us!

44:06.680 --> 44:11.420
Captain Hook comes out of his cabin and sees Peter Pan.

44:12.360 --> 44:15.480
He and his pirates are very angry.

44:16.320 --> 44:23.660
Hook takes his long sword and says, I'm going to fight you, Peter Pan.

44:24.420 --> 44:30.590
This is your last fight because tonight you're going to die.

44:30.640 --> 44:30.820
Die!

44:32.720 --> 44:37.360
Hook fights with his long sword and with his big hook.

44:38.260 --> 44:42.360
Peter is very brave and fights with his small sword.

44:43.520 --> 44:45.560
He pushes Hook to the back of the ship.

44:46.680 --> 44:47.780
It is a terrible fight.

44:48.960 --> 44:52.520
John, Michael and the lost boys fight the pirates.

44:53.560 --> 44:58.460
After a long fight, they throw the pirates into the sea.

44:59.880 --> 45:03.980
Peter and Captain Hook fight all over the ship.

45:05.140 --> 45:06.800
Their swords make a lot of noise.

45:07.740 --> 45:11.080
Suddenly, Peter pushes Captain Hook into the sea.

45:11.940 --> 45:15.140
Hook shouts, Oh no!

45:16.700 --> 45:22.500
He falls into the sea and into the mouth of the hungry crocodile.

45:23.080 --> 45:24.420
Everyone cheers!

45:25.720 --> 45:29.260
Oh Peter! Says Wendy happily.

45:29.920 --> 45:32.120
You're a very brave boy.

45:33.040 --> 45:36.200
She smiles and kisses him on the cheek.

45:37.500 --> 45:42.740
Peter is happy and says, Now the Jolly Roger is ours!

45:43.800 --> 45:44.780
We can go home!

45:46.380 --> 45:46.980
Home!

45:48.000 --> 45:49.060
Everyone shouts.

45:50.220 --> 45:51.280
Let's go!

45:55.160 --> 46:04.080
Chapter 7 Back in London The Darling home in London is a very sad place.

46:04.640 --> 46:08.360
Mr. and Mrs. Darling never smile or laugh.

46:09.260 --> 46:13.300
They always think about Wendy, John and Michael.

46:14.540 --> 46:23.260
Every morning at breakfast, Mrs. Darling looks at the three empty chairs and says, Where are my children?

46:24.760 --> 46:26.300
She has tears in her eyes.

46:27.760 --> 46:31.880
Nanna goes to the nursery and sees three empty beds.

46:32.900 --> 46:40.600
In the evening, Mr. Darling comes home after work and he does not hear his children talking and laughing.

46:42.280 --> 46:47.070
Mrs. Darling often sits in the silent nursery and cries.

46:47.120 --> 46:53.400
She thinks of her children, their games and their happy voices.

46:54.720 --> 47:00.020
Nanna tries to comfort her, but nothing can make Mrs. Darling happy.

47:01.240 --> 47:04.320
She always leaves the nursery window open.

47:06.020 --> 47:09.700
Then one night, something wonderful happens.

47:10.880 --> 47:21.460
Wendy, John and Michael fly into the nursery Mrs. Darling is sitting near the fireplace and thinking about her children.

47:22.220 --> 47:24.320
She hears a voice and turns around.

47:24.920 --> 47:28.100
Mother! Mother! cries Wendy happily.

47:28.680 --> 47:29.240
We home!

47:30.280 --> 47:33.220
Mrs. Darling sees Wendy, John and Michael.

47:34.240 --> 47:35.260
She is very surprised.

47:36.400 --> 47:37.840
She cannot believe her eyes.

47:38.800 --> 47:39.480
Oh!

47:40.820 --> 47:41.820
She cries.

47:42.920 --> 47:47.200
Is this true or is it a dream?

47:48.680 --> 47:49.660
Mother!

47:50.520 --> 47:52.120
The children say.

47:53.500 --> 47:54.500
It's true!

47:55.760 --> 47:56.920
We're home!

47:57.960 --> 48:00.980
They hug their mother and kiss her.

48:01.760 --> 48:08.850
It's wonderful to see you! Says Mrs. Darling, looking at her three children.

48:08.900 --> 48:11.800
Oh, let me look at you.

48:12.640 --> 48:15.880
How wonderful to hear your sweet voices.

48:16.820 --> 48:20.240
Nanna runs into the nursery and barks happily.

48:24.900 --> 48:28.420
The children are very pleased to see her.

48:29.160 --> 48:32.800
I must call your father. Says Mrs. Darling.

48:34.040 --> 48:38.240
George, George, come to the nursery immediately.

48:38.900 --> 48:43.760
Mr. Darling comes to the nursery and sees his three children.

48:44.220 --> 48:48.560
Oh, this is a wonderful night.

48:49.240 --> 48:50.160
He says happily.

48:50.960 --> 48:53.820
Our children are finally home.

48:54.900 --> 48:56.820
Mother! Says Wendy.

48:58.260 --> 49:01.000
Peter Pan and the lost boys are here too.

49:01.820 --> 49:03.000
They're waiting outside.

49:04.720 --> 49:08.700
Ask them to come inside. Says Mrs. Darling.

49:09.660 --> 49:17.460
The six lost boys slowly enter the nursery and look at Mr. and Mrs. Darling and Nanna.

49:18.420 --> 49:20.360
Mother? Says Wendy.

49:21.240 --> 49:23.060
These are the lost boys.

49:23.980 --> 49:26.960
They haven't got a family or a mother.

49:27.920 --> 49:29.360
Can they stay with us?

49:30.000 --> 49:39.580
Oh, these dear little boys haven't got a family or a mother. Says Mrs. Darling.

49:40.160 --> 49:43.180
Of course they can stay with us.

49:43.960 --> 49:46.100
We're their new family.

49:47.140 --> 49:52.080
Thank you Mrs. Darling. Say the lost boys.

49:53.180 --> 49:59.700
But where is Peter Pan? asks Mrs. Darling, looking around the nursery.

50:01.040 --> 50:08.420
Peter Pan comes into the nursery and says, Here I am, but I don't want to stay here.

50:09.240 --> 50:16.300
Everyone is surprised, and Mrs. Darling asks, Why don't you want to stay here?

50:17.040 --> 50:21.860
I don't want to go to school and learn things. Says Peter.

50:22.440 --> 50:24.150
I don't want to grow up.

50:24.200 --> 50:28.980
I want to be a young boy and have lots of fun forever.

50:30.080 --> 50:33.360
But Peter. Says Wendy sadly.

50:34.240 --> 50:37.420
I must go back to Neverland. Says Peter.

50:38.160 --> 50:41.100
My home and my friends are there.

50:41.960 --> 50:45.460
I'm happy with the Indians and the fairies.

50:46.340 --> 50:52.260
Wendy is surprised and asks, When can I see you then?

50:53.200 --> 50:59.480
Mrs. Darling thinks for a moment and says, I have a good idea.

51:00.140 --> 51:05.020
Wendy, you can visit Peter in Neverland every spring.

51:05.800 --> 51:08.060
You can stay there for a week.

51:09.920 --> 51:14.720
Can I really go to Neverland every spring mother? asks Wendy.

51:15.660 --> 51:20.640
Of course you can. Says Mrs. Darling, smiling.

51:21.460 --> 51:26.180
Peter looks at Mrs. Darling and asks, Is that a promise?

51:27.000 --> 51:30.020
Of course it is. Says Mrs. Darling.

51:30.780 --> 51:35.220
Then I want spring to come quickly. Says Peter happily.

51:36.480 --> 51:37.280
Yes.

51:37.960 --> 51:40.940
Very quickly. Says Wendy laughing.

51:41.860 --> 51:44.280
Come on Tink. Says Peter.

51:44.800 --> 51:47.900
Let's fly home and wait for spring.

51:49.000 --> 51:55.500
Peter Pan and Tinkerbell fly out of the nursery window and into the night sky.

51:56.800 --> 51:59.340
They are flying to Neverland.

52:02.620 --> 52:03.840
Exercise three.

52:04.940 --> 52:08.540
Wendy is taking the Lost Boys on a short tour of London.

52:09.560 --> 52:11.960
She is giving them some information about the city.

52:13.060 --> 52:16.180
Listen to her and then choose the correct answer.

52:18.040 --> 52:22.920
Today we are going to visit some interesting places in London.

52:23.980 --> 52:31.240
The first place we are going to see is Big Ben, the big clock tower near the houses of Parliament.

52:32.480 --> 52:35.420
Look at the clock at the top of the tower.

52:36.720 --> 52:39.660
Now we are going to travel on the River Thames.

52:40.660 --> 52:41.890
Let's buy tickets.

52:41.940 --> 52:45.800
It's always fun to ride a boat on the river.

52:47.320 --> 52:49.360
We are going to see Tower Bridge.

52:50.520 --> 52:55.180
The bridge sometimes opens up to let big ships pass.

52:56.760 --> 53:00.200
The Tower of London is near Tower Bridge.

53:01.160 --> 53:04.560
It's very old and a lot of people visit it.

53:05.900 --> 53:08.790
Let's walk by this beautiful church.

53:08.840 --> 53:11.000
It's St Paul's Cathedral.

53:12.200 --> 53:14.680
The people of London love this church.

53:15.760 --> 53:19.740
Oh, it's a quarter past one and time for lunch.

53:20.620 --> 53:23.580
After lunch we are going to Hyde Park.

53:24.520 --> 53:26.460
It's a wonderful big park.

53:27.400 --> 53:30.320
We can play there until half past four.

53:31.220 --> 53:32.960
Then we must go home for tea.

53:36.100 --> 53:37.440
The Darling Home.

53:38.440 --> 53:41.620
What does the Darling Home in London look like?

53:42.340 --> 53:45.400
It is a comfortable home with a nice garden.

53:46.480 --> 53:49.300
On the ground floor there is a dining room.

53:50.280 --> 53:51.960
The family has its meals here.

53:53.100 --> 53:56.380
There is a long table with a lot of chairs around it.

53:57.300 --> 53:59.450
There are also pictures on the walls.

53:59.500 --> 54:07.760
On the ground floor there is also a large sitting room with a big sofa and comfortable chairs.

54:08.720 --> 54:12.500
People sit here in the evening and read or talk.

54:13.720 --> 54:15.320
They also listen to music.

54:16.780 --> 54:18.860
Families like singing together.

54:19.740 --> 54:21.440
Often someone plays the piano.

54:22.520 --> 54:25.740
When friends come to visit they sit in the sitting room.

54:26.600 --> 54:30.060
At the back of the house there is a big kitchen.

54:31.300 --> 54:36.000
Next to the kitchen there is a small room called the Scullery.

54:37.000 --> 54:39.080
This is where the servants wash up.

54:40.740 --> 54:44.800
Some big houses have breakfast rooms and libraries.

54:46.220 --> 54:51.380
On the first floor there are the bedrooms, the bathroom and the nursery.

54:52.380 --> 54:54.920
The rooms have open fireplaces.

54:56.280 --> 54:59.900
The servants live in rooms at the top of the house.
